  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "title": "Int-keyed fields silently dropped; duplicate int-keyed fields not reported",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "In the field-handling branch, the guard is missing \u0027!\u0027: line 1163 adds an int-keyed field only when its key is already present, but the first occurrence is never added (line 1163 is false), so ContainsKey never becomes true. As a result every int-keyed field is silently omitted from the serialization model and duplicate int-keyed fields never reach line 1154\u2019s KeysMustBeUnique diagnostic (no MsgPack005, no crash, silent data omission). The equivalent property branch correctly uses \u0027if (!intMembers.ContainsKey(...))\u0027 at line 1023; the base code added unconditionally at line 1155, so head regresses field handling versus base as well.",
